@@ -70,6 +70,14 @@ Order links live in a SQLite file (`data.db` in the project root, overridable wi
 
 The repository includes `railway.toml` so Railway can build the app with `npm ci && npm run build`, start it with `npm run start`, and use `/api/health` as the deployment health check.
 
+Optional Print Operations **Tools** link — Pricing Matrix:
+
+```text
+PRICING_MATRIX_URL=https://<tabletop-pricing-matrix>.up.railway.app
+```
+
+When set, a **Price** tool appears in the sidebar Tools section and opens the quote generator.
+
 For the initial single-service setup:
 
 1. Connect the GitHub repository to a Railway service and deploy the `main` branch.
